<rdf:Description rdf:about="">
<dc:identifier></dc:identifier>
<dc:title>Consensus control for distributed power tracking by device-level digital twin agents</dc:title>
<prism:doi></prism:doi>
<prism:url></prism:url>
<dc:creator><rdf:Bag><rdf:li>Yanan Wang</rdf:li>
<rdf:li>Zhimin Guo</rdf:li>
<rdf:li>Yuhang Pang</rdf:li>
<rdf:li>Kaiqiang Gao</rdf:li>
<rdf:li>Jian Zhao</rdf:li>
</rdf:Bag></dc:creator>
<dc:description>Abstract: The development of electronics and software has resulted in the ability of twin agents to act as digital counterparts for the optimization, control, and monitoring of real power grids.</dc:description>
<dc:subject><rdf:Bag><rdf:li>digital twins</rdf:li><rdf:li>consensus control</rdf:li><rdf:li>distributed optimization</rdf:li><rdf:li>power tracking</rdf:li><rdf:li>physical-model simulation</rdf:li></rdf:Bag></dc:subject>
